# Slack updates for GitHub activity

After a commit is pushed, a pull request is opened, or a pull request is merged, post one short update to Slack `#github-activity` (`C0C4SPGR8AV`).

Covered repositories:

- `signet7-io/signet7`
- `signet7-io/signet7-core`
- `signet7-io/signet7-web`
- `signet7-io/signet7-active`
- `signet7-io/team-skills`

Do not post activity from `signet7-io/signet7-history` or `ClubSanderson/Cardwise`.

Post only after that GitHub action succeeds. Skip the post if that same commit, pull request, or merge was already announced. A squash merge that also updates `main` is one merge post, not a second commit post.

Lead with the event. Include the repository, the pull request number or commit subject, the title, the link, and the author. Do not include secrets, tokens, or credentials.

```text
**Pull request merged** — signet7-web #214

site: use collapsible categories in the handbook navigation
https://github.com/signet7-io/signet7-web/pull/214
Justin
```

Channel: https://signet7-team.slack.com/archives/C0C4SPGR8AV
